.TH SYSLINUXOS-WIFI-ANALYZER 1 "October 2026" "SysLinuxOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syslinuxos-wifi-analyzer \- discover and locate WiFi access points
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syslinuxos-wifi-analyzer
.RB [ --demo ]
.RB [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select a WiFi adapter and start scanning. Select a radio by its BSSID and open
Segnale to track its frequency using a signal gauge, recent history and peak.
Enable Bip attivo for audible feedback. Stronger received signal produces
more frequent beeps. Sensitivity and volume are adjustable.
.PP
The GUI runs as the desktop user. A restricted helper requests authorization
through polkit for iw scanning. No network service is started.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Display explicitly simulated observations without scanning or authorization.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version and exit.
.SH LIMITATIONS
RSSI is not distance or direction. Reflections and metal structures can move
the strongest reception point. Walk slowly and cross the candidate area from
two directions while keeping receiver height and orientation constant.
.PP
Missing or stale samples and scan errors suspend audible feedback.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/syslinuxos-wifi-analyzer/
.SH AUTHOR
Franco Conidi. BSS parsing adapted from Sparrow WiFi by ghostop14.
